Overview of the business case
What is the system about?
A crowdfunding platform is a web system where creators publish fundraising projects, and supporters make donations (payments) to help projects reach their goal amount before the deadline. Supporters can also leave comments and receive rewards offered by the project owner.

Primary users

Visitors/Supporters (donors): browse projects, donate, comment.

Creators (project owners): create projects, define rewards, monitor donations.

Administrators: manage categories, payment methods, handle fraud/complaints (optional for future extension).

Primary goals / problems solved

Help creators raise money transparently with clear goals and deadlines.

Let donors support projects safely via tracked payments and statuses.

Provide community interaction via comments and reward offerings.

Maintain accurate financial tracking (donations, fees, payment method).

